  "description": "It's easy to look past carrots when the farmers market is overflowing with tomatoes and corn, but don't: They're in season this time of year too, and are deserving of a spot on the summertime table. Here, beautiful sweet carrots are lightly cooked, then tossed in a flavorful dressing that's rich with ginger, cilantro, lemon, and just a touch of tahini.",
  "notes": "Notes: Small, slender young carrots are particularly beautiful in this dish and can be cooked whole, but any size carrot will work as long as you cut it into spears of about 1/2-inch in diameter before cooking. If you use young carrots with very thin skins, scrubbing them is enough; if they're larger and older, you can peel the skins before cooking.",
